 ◈ Thematic breaks                                                              
 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── 
                                                                                
 Three spellings, all of which must draw the same rule:                         
                                                                                
              ─────────────────────────◈──────────────────────────              
                                                                                
              ─────────────────────────◈──────────────────────────              
                                                                                
              ─────────────────────────◈──────────────────────────              
                                                                                
 ◈ Paragraph edge cases                                                         
 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── 
                                                                                
 A paragraph immediately followed by a heading with no blank line is not legal  
 Markdown, but a paragraph containing a very long unbreakable token is, and     
 this is one: supercalifragilisticexpialidociousantidisestablishmentarianism.   
                                                                                
 A     paragraph     with     runs     of     internal     whitespace     that  
 must collapse to single spaces.                                                
                                                                                
 [1] The first footnote body.                                                   
                                                                                
 [2] The second footnote body, long enough to wrap at eighty columns so the     
     continuation indent can be inspected.                                      
                                                                                
 [3] A footnote with a name rather than a number.
